"- Object 1 Hazelnut\n    - Attribute 1 Type - A single, whole hazelnut with a smooth, rounded, and slightly tapered shape, featuring a distinct cap at the top.\n    - Attribute 2 Color - Rich, warm brown with variations in tone; the main body is a medium to deep brown, while the cap is a darker, textured brown with lighter, fibrous patterns.\n    - Attribute 3 Size - Approximately 2 to 3 centimeters in length and 1.5 to 2.5 centimeters in width, with a generally ovoid form.\n    - Attribute 4 Material - Hard, woody shell with a smooth, slightly glossy surface on the body and a rough, fibrous texture on the cap.\n    - Attribute 5 Composition - Composed of a single, intact nut shell encasing the edible kernel, with a fibrous, leaf-like cap at the apex.\n    - Attribute 6 Quantity - One.\n    - Attribute 7 Relative Location - Positioned centrally in the frame, occupying the majority of the visual space.\n    - Attribute 8 Orientation - The hazelnut is oriented with its cap facing upward and slightly angled toward the viewer, showing the top and side profile.\n    - Attribute 9 Connection or Attachments - The cap is attached to the main body at the top, forming a natural, seamless junction with no visible seams or external attachments."